# REQUIRES: cuda
# The check of the extents of the writer of a list of units
# (D422; D417, Section 8, S4a): after the positions of
# a step every place of a unit must lie within its covering radius
# (Inputs/segments_writer.py). Two frames: the first builds the list, the
# writer of the second checks it.
#   - ok: every place within its radius, the site of a kind of weights
#     (1.8, -0.4, -0.4) 0.047 nm from its anchor; the run ends.
#   - convex: a hydrogen of a water 0.11 nm from its oxygen, beyond the
#     kind's 0.09582 nm: a frame atom, which covers every site whose
#     weights lie in [0, 1] (the convex rule).
#   - hull: the site of weights (3, -1, -1) 0.117 nm from its anchor, beyond
#     the kind's 0.1 nm, with its frame atoms within it: a site outside the
#     hull of its frame, which the writer forms and checks itself.
#   - anchor: an anchored member of the rest 0.12 nm from its anchor,
#     beyond rho = 0.10901 nm.
# Each probe fails when its check is removed (tried once each and reverted):
# without the check of a frame atom the convex probe ends, with every site
# taken as convex the hull probe ends, and without the check of an anchored
# member the anchor probe ends; the others still stop.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/ok %t/convex %t/hull %t/anchor
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py ok %t/ok
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/ok/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py convex %t/convex
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/convex/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | not mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py hull %t/hull
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/hull/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | not mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py anchor %t/anchor
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/anchor/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | not mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: a unit of the list of units lies beyond its covering radius after the constraints of a step
#
# The direction of the test of the reference points in f32 with its counted
# margin: eight waters moved whole by zeta (1 + 2^-23), zeta = 0.05 nm the
# least half-margin of the segments, must build the list again; moved by
# zeta (1 - 2^-10), farther inside than the counted margin, must not. The
# directions of the first are chosen so that the f32 test without its margin
# (z = zeta, c = 1) passes every one of them, as the generator's simulation
# of the kernel's arithmetic prints: with the margin removed from the
# kernel (tried once and reverted) the list is not built again.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/beyond/dumps %t/inside/dumps
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py beyond %t/beyond | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SIMBEYOND
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/beyond/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu="dump-segments=true" --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | env MDRT_SEGMENTS_DUMP=%t/beyond/dumps mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py builds %t/beyond/dumps | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BEYOND
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py inside %t/inside | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SIMINSIDE
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/inside/harness.mlir --convert-md-exec-to-gpu="dump-segments=true" --convert-md-alg-to-gpu \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_gpu_to_llvm \
# RUN: | env MDRT_SEGMENTS_DUMP=%t/inside/dumps mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils,%mdrt,%mdrt_cuda
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/segments_writer.py builds %t/inside/dumps | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INSIDE
# SIMBEYOND: beyond: of 8 units, the f32 test passes 0 with its counted margin and 8 without it
# SIMINSIDE: inside: of 8 units, the f32 test passes 8 with its counted margin and 8 without it
# BEYOND: builds 2
# INSIDE: builds 1
